// Rule: [T1059.004][T1036] Amos - Hidden Application Support Execution
// MITRE ATT&CK: T1059.004, T1036
// Classification: Hunting query
// Status: Untested implementation sketch
// Primary platform: Microsoft Defender XDR
// Required telemetry: DeviceProcessEvents
// Purpose: Hunts for AccountsHelper or mdworker_shared executing from the two hidden Apple-lookalike Application Support directories observed in the Unit 42 lab infection.
// Logic: Evaluate DeviceProcessEvents for hidden application support execution using the existing source-derived conditions while preserving projected investigation context.
// A match proves: A result proves that the published query conditions matched in DeviceProcessEvents; it is an investigative event, not a malicious verdict.
// A match does not prove: successful exploitation, malicious ownership, downstream impact, campaign attribution or complete compromise without corroborating evidence.
// Expected false positives: authorized administration, approved software, testing, or benign artifact collisions.
// Coverage limits: local schema, field population, retention, collection scope, and attacker variation require validation.
// Evidence claims: C001, C002, C003
//
// AMOS execution from hidden Apple-lookalike Application Support directories
// Hunting query - Untested implementation sketch
// Primary platform: Microsoft Defender XDR Advanced Hunting
// Required telemetry: Microsoft Defender for Endpoint on macOS -> DeviceProcessEvents
// Confidence: Medium
// A match establishes execution of a source-observed artifact, not credential theft or exfiltration.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where
    (FileName == "AccountsHelper" and
     FolderPath endswith "/Library/Application Support/.com.apple.accountsd")
    or
    (FileName == "mdworker_shared" and
     FolderPath endswith "/Library/Application Support/.com.apple.metadata.mds")
| project Timestamp, DeviceId, DeviceName, AccountName,
          FileName, FolderPath, ProcessCommandLine,
          InitiatingProcessFileName, InitiatingProcessCommandLine,
          SHA1, SHA256, ReportId
| order by Timestamp desc
